<!--
  CLASS NEGATIVE for clause 8.7.1.1: the device class is Display ('mntr'), not
  ColorSpace.

  A conformant v4 three-component matrix-based Display profile carrying a
  conforming PQ cicpTag and HDR Image metadata.  Every other membership
  condition of 8.7.1.1 is satisfied, so this fixture isolates the class
  condition alone: a classifier that stopped testing it would report this
  profile as an HDR ColorSpace Profile and would still pass every positive in
  the corpus.  HdrInputDisplayMeta is the 'scnr' half of the same pair, so
  neither surviving non-ColorSpace class can be admitted by a classifier that
  tests only one of them.

  THE AMENDMENT SAYS THIS IN AS MANY WORDS.  Its Introduction and its Issues
  section both address exactly this shape: a Display or Input profile carrying
  cicpTag and HAGC "is functionally similar, in terms of tone-mapping
  capability, to an HDR ColorSpace Profile under this clause, but is not one:
  it does not carry the guarantees of 8.7.1.1 and 8.7.1.2".  The profile is a
  perfectly ordinary Display profile and nothing is reported against it.

  THIS FIXTURE WAS THE CONFORMING BASE of the corpus under clause 8.10, where
  the sub-class was built on the Input and Display classes.  It is unchanged
  in intent and inverted in verdict, as HdrColorSpaceClass - now the positive
  - is inverted the other way.

  IT KEEPS ITS COLORANT TAGS, deliberately and unlike every 'spac' fixture
  here: it is a matrix-based Display profile, 8.4.3 defines those tags for it,
  and it is the fixture the registry's "primaries code 2 resolves against the
  containing profile's matrix column tags" rule is tested against in
  hdr-profile-classification.cpp.  An HDR ColorSpace Profile has no such tags,
  which is PROPOSAL-ISSUE HDR-18 and is asserted alongside it.

  THE HDR DISPLAY ENTRIES ARE GONE.  DERH, DCV and DRWL and their headroom
  precedence were clause 8.10.5, which the 23-09-2026 revision deletes:
  physical display characterization is out of scope for the sub-class.  The
  HDR Image entries - CRWL, CLL, MDCV - are registered and unaffected, and are
  what this fixture still exercises.

  EXPECTED CLASSIFICATION is icHdrProfileHdrContent - NOT icHdrProfileNone.
  The profile carries HDR Image metadata and a PQ cicpTag, which is precisely
  what the middle bucket of icHdrProfileClass exists for: HDR content a
  consumer may legitimately act on, in a profile that is not an HDR ColorSpace
  Profile.  A classifier reduced to a yes/no could not express this verdict at
  all, which is the second thing these fixtures pin.
-->
<IccProfile>
  <Header>
    <PreferredCMMType>ICCD</PreferredCMMType>
    <ProfileVersion>4.50</ProfileVersion>
    <ProfileDeviceClass>mntr</ProfileDeviceClass>
    <DataColourSpace>RGB </DataColourSpace>
    <PCS>XYZ </PCS>
    <CreationDateTime>2026-08-05T00:00:00</CreationDateTime>
    <ProfileFlags EmbeddedInFile="false" UseWithEmbeddedDataOnly="false"/>
    <DeviceAttributes ReflectiveOrTransparency="reflective" GlossyOrMatte="glossy" MediaPolarity="positive" MediaColour="colour"/>
    <RenderingIntent>Relative Colorimetric</RenderingIntent>
    <PCSIlluminant>
      <XYZNumber X="0.964202880859" Y="1.000000000000" Z="0.824905395508"/>
    </PCSIlluminant>
    <ProfileCreator>ICCD</ProfileCreator>
  </Header>
  <Tags>
    <redColorantTag> <XYZArrayType>
      <XYZNumber X="0.436004638672" Y="0.222503662109" Z="0.013900756836"/>
    </XYZArrayType> </redColorantTag>

    <greenColorantTag> <XYZArrayType>
      <XYZNumber X="0.385101318359" Y="0.716903686523" Z="0.097106933594"/>
    </XYZArrayType> </greenColorantTag>

    <blueColorantTag> <XYZArrayType>
      <XYZNumber X="0.143096923828" Y="0.060592651367" Z="0.713897705078"/>
    </XYZArrayType> </blueColorantTag>

    <!-- Standard Bradford D65 to D50 adaptation. -->
    <chromaticAdaptationTag> <s15Fixed16ArrayType>
      <Array>
        1.047882  0.022919 -0.050201
        0.029587  0.990479 -0.017059
       -0.009232  0.015076  0.751678
      </Array>
    </s15Fixed16ArrayType> </chromaticAdaptationTag>

    <mediaWhitePointTag> <XYZArrayType>
      <XYZNumber X="0.964202880859" Y="1.000000000000" Z="0.824905395508"/>
    </XYZArrayType> </mediaWhitePointTag>

    <cicpTag> <cicpType>
      <cicpFields ColorPrimaries="1" TransferCharacteristics="16" MatrixCoefficients="0" VideoFullRangeFlag="1"/>
    </cicpType> </cicpTag>

    <metaDataTag> <dictType>
      <DictEntry Name="CRWL" Value="203.0"/>
      <DictEntry Name="CLL" Value="1000.0 400.0 9"/>
      <DictEntry Name="MDCV" Value="1000.0 0.005 9"/>
    </dictType> </metaDataTag>

    <!-- There are no TRC tags and no matrix column tags, and under the
         23-09-2026 revision that is not a prohibition being obeyed - it is
         what a ColorSpace profile IS. 8.7 never defines either set for this
         class, so, in the revision's words, "there is nothing for this
         amendment to prohibit". The transfer comes from the cicpTag's
         TransferCharacteristics field and the primaries from its
         ColourPrimaries field; 8.7.1.1 says the cicpTag "is the only tag that
         can convey either".

         The AToB0Tag/BToA0Tag pair below is required by 8.7 of every
         ColorSpace profile, which 8.7.1.5 leans on rather than restates -
         "both already unconditionally required of every ColorSpace profile by
         8.7" - and it is what gives a legacy CMM a rendering path. Identity B
         curves: these fixtures exercise classification and the tone-mapping
         chain, not the bake's accuracy. -->

    <AToB0Tag> <lutAtoBType>
      <Channels InputChannels="3" OutputChannels="3"/>
      <BCurves>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
      </BCurves>
    </lutAtoBType> </AToB0Tag>

    <BToA0Tag> <lutBtoAType>
      <Channels InputChannels="3" OutputChannels="3"/>
      <BCurves>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
        <Curve IdentitySize="2"/>
      </BCurves>
    </lutBtoAType> </BToA0Tag>

    <profileDescriptionTag> <multiLocalizedUnicodeType>
      <LocalizedText LanguageCountry="enUS"><![CDATA[iccDEV HDR display profile with HDR Image and HDR Display metadata]]></LocalizedText>
    </multiLocalizedUnicodeType> </profileDescriptionTag>

    <copyrightTag> <multiLocalizedUnicodeType>
      <LocalizedText LanguageCountry="enUS"><![CDATA[Copyright (C) 2026 The International Color Consortium. Generated fixture, no measured data.]]></LocalizedText>
    </multiLocalizedUnicodeType> </copyrightTag>
  </Tags>
</IccProfile>
